 # VoxelGrid from Mesh (Ray Method)
 Also called: CUDA Mesh Voxelizer, Mesh to Particle Cloud Conversion, Raycasting-based Voxelization, X-ray Voxelization
 
 ## Overview
-This method converts a 3D triangle mesh into a discrete voxel grid by casting rays from voxel centers to determine occupancy. It distinguishes itself from rasterization-based siblings by relying on geometric intersection tests rather than screen-space projection, allowing it to robustly handle arbitrary mesh orientations and generate solid volumes or signed distance fields (SDFs) [S2, S3]. It solves the problem of converting continuous surface representations into discrete volumetric data suitable for volume rendering or 3D printing [S1].
